    <item>
      <title>Squeak 2.23.2</title>
      <pubDate>Wed, 11 Nov 2026 09:04:52 +0000</pubDate>
      <sparkle:version>22302</sparkle:version>
      <sparkle:shortVersionString>2.23.2</sparkle:shortVersionString>
      <sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>14.0</sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>
      <description><![CDATA[<!DOCTYPE html><html><head><meta charset="utf-8"><style>html{color-scheme:light dark}body{font:13px/1.5 -apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'SF Pro Text',system-ui,sans-serif;color:#18181b;background:transparent;margin:0;padding:4px 2px}ul{margin:0 0 10px;padding-left:18px}li{margin:0 0 6px}p{margin:0 0 10px}h4{font-size:12px;font-weight:600;color:#52525b;margin:16px 0 6px;padding-top:10px;border-top:1px solid rgba(0,0,0,.08)}code{font:12px ui-monospace,'SF Mono',monospace;background:rgba(0,0,0,.06);padding:1px 4px;border-radius:6px}@media (prefers-color-scheme:dark){body{color:#f4f4f5}h4{color:#a1a1aa;border-top-color:rgba(255,255,255,.12)}code{background:rgba(255,255,255,.1)}}</style></head><body><ul><li>If setup can't start the background service, Squeak says why and offers Send report with the details attached (secrets removed).</li><li>Reporting a problem is easier everywhere: a Report button beside every Try again, a gentle offer when something fails, and reports know your Squeak account so the team can reply.</li></ul><h4>Also in 2.23.1</h4><ul><li>Setup on a new Mac no longer hangs on starting the background service. It asks to run in the background first, says what it is doing at each step, and if something goes wrong it tells you why with Try again, Copy details and Show log.</li></ul><h4>Also in 2.23.0</h4><ul><li>New words that fit the pond: a pond's working folders are <strong>streams</strong> (their git branch shown beside them) and an agent's helpers are <strong>ducklings</strong>.</li><li>Every thread is a duck in its own colour, the same on your Mac and iPhone, with a small Claude or Codex badge.</li><li>New streams get names like Mossy Creek or Recursive Mallard; New stream suggests one and can roll another.</li><li>Signing in is a page in Squeak's window. Squeak comes back to the front when you finish in the browser.</li><li>Every thread's agent knows it runs in Squeak, and knows who is talking when several people write in one thread.</li></ul><ul><li>Shared threads show the machine they run on, while local threads keep their own branch and routing.</li><li>Pond settings has clearer sections and shortcuts, wrapping colour choices, an Add label button and collapsible action prompts.</li><li>Dropdowns stay close to the control you clicked, highlight it while open, and stay attached when the window resizes.</li></ul></body></html>]]></description>
